title: 'M1.3 round 2 (H1): separate the probe helper by identifier and group, pin production by a version floor; the team wildcard limits what code can separate'
summary: 'The probe helper now signs as gnomon.probe into SW4BMQ8PNL.gnomon.probe and refuses production names; production keys moved to SW4BMQ8PNL.gnomon.prod and the build signs exactly that group. The kernel pins identifier+team plus info protocol and MIN_HELPER_VERSION, checked on the running child after a pid code-sign check; a CDHash allowlist was rejected because timestamped signatures change it every founder build. Residual: the Developer ID profile grants SW4BMQ8PNL.*, so any team-signed binary with that profile can claim .prod; real separation needs its own App ID and profile for the production helper.'
